legalExplanation:
The **NSCDC Act, 2003, section 3(1)(c)–(d)** gives the Corps power to:
- inspect the premises of private guard companies and their training facilities, and approve them if they meet the standard;
- supervise and monitor the activities of all private guard companies and keep a register for that purpose;
- organise workshops and training for private guard companies;
- seal up any private guard company operating without a valid licence.

This is part of the Corps' mandate to regulate the private security industry. It does not give NSCDC power to search residents' homes or arrest residents simply because a guard company is being inspected.
